From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: describe the fuel gauge

Nothing described the fuel gauge, so the only battery information came from
the charger, leaving charge level, capacity, current and temperature
unreported.

The stock device tree places it at address 0x55 on the eighth QUP serial
engine, alongside the fast-charge microcontroller. That engine is i2c8 here
and was not enabled. It is described without GPI DMA and at 100 kHz, matching
what i2c4 already needs on this board.

The stock name for the part is bq27541, but its registers are not laid out
that way. Reading them directly with the driver unbound shows state of charge
at 0x1c reporting 100, temperature at 0x02 reporting 33.9 C, remaining and
full charge capacity at 0x0c and 0x0e, and current at 0x10 reading zero on a
full battery. That is the bq27421 layout, not the bq27541 one, where state of
charge would sit at 0x2c and temperature at 0x06. Reading it as a bq27541
returned a state of charge within a few counts of the voltage and a cycle
count identical to the remaining capacity, because 0x2a and 0x2c hold
something else entirely on this part.

Describe it as ti,bq27411, which shares that register map and correctly
declares cycle count as unavailable rather than reporting a neighbouring
register.

monitored-battery is deliberately omitted. The gauge is factory programmed for
the cell it ships with, and the driver can push devicetree values into a
gauge's data memory, which is not something a description should do to a
working battery.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -363,6 +363,18 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&i2c8 {
+	/delete-property/ dmas;
+	/delete-property/ dma-names;
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	fuel-gauge@55 {
+		compatible = "ti,bq27411";
+		reg = <0x55>;
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c17 {
 	status = "okay";
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
--
2.50.1
